PROSE:
With the feral overseer deleted and the node collapsing into digital dust, the party scrambled to find the vault before the 30-second purge timer hit zero. 

[System Alert: Frontier Zone Purge Initiated. Time Remaining: 30s.]

The Inner Office was tearing itself apart. The catastrophic default had stripped the room's structural integrity, causing the polished obsidian desk to fracture and the ceiling to rain heavy chunks of masonry. Rhea Mercer’s lungs burned with a dry, metallic heat. 

[Stamina: 0/150]
[Status Effect: Exhaustion (Severe) - Movement speed reduced by 75%.]

Zero stamina wasn't just a number; it was a physical weight. The System punished empty resource bars by turning blood into sludge and muscles into lead. Every step toward the back wall required a conscious, agonizing exertion of will. In her left hand, the *Mercy Cache Coordinates* pulsed with a frantic, mythic-tier golden light, practically vibrating against her palm. She kept the *Administrative Residue Token* and the rest of her exploit gear stowed safely in her left blazer pocket, unwilling to risk dropping them in the chaos.

"Move!" Vance Harrow roared. 

[HP: 2/100]
[Status Effect: Heavy Blunt-Force Trauma.]

Vance was a walking corpse. He leaned heavily on his *Rebar*, gripping the weapon in his right hand as if it were the only thing anchoring his soul to his body. His blistered hands were white-knuckled, the iron shaft trembling under his weight. He deflected a falling slab of marble with a desperate swing, the impact sending a violent shudder up his arm, but the rebar held. 

[Warning: Chassis Integrity at 34%. Critical System Failure Imminent.]

Unit 734 whirred past them, its smoking chassis venting thick plumes of caustic black exhaust. The drone's optical lens flickered erratically, projecting the red countdown timer directly onto the cracking stone floor. 

[Time Remaining: 18s.]

"Where is the terminal?" Rhea shouted over the deafening grind of collapsing architecture. 

"Behind the tapestry!" Unit 734 synthesized, its voice box glitching into a high-pitched squeal. "Administrative bypass required!"

Vance didn't wait for instructions. He lunged forward, dragging his battered body across the shaking floor, and ripped the heavy velvet tapestry from the wall with his free hand. Behind it, a sleek, recessed wall terminal blinked with an angry red lock icon. 

[Time Remaining: 12s.]

Rhea slammed into the wall next to the terminal. Her vision swam, the edges of the room tunneling into darkness as the exhaustion debuff threatened to force her into unconsciousness. She forced her eyes open, lifting her left hand. The *Mercy Cache Coordinates* flared, the digital string of numbers and runes unwinding from the mythic item. 

"Input it!" Vance yelled, watching the ceiling above them bow inward. Dust poured down in thick sheets. 

Rhea smashed the glowing coordinates into the terminal's receptor slot. 

[Validating Administrative Override...]
[Time Remaining: 6s.]
[Coordinates Accepted. Access Granted.]

The wall terminal flashed a brilliant, blinding green. 

The heavy stone panel grinds open, revealing the dark threshold of the vault just as a massive support beam crashes behind them. The hidden vault opens, revealing the Mercy Cache as the ceiling caves in.

